{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"862c2db98ed511b0","name":"card_unit_sunrise_division","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/WorldAtWar/units/card_unit_sunrise_division","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SUNRISE DIVISION","text":"Deployment: Gets +6+6 if your HQ has 10 or less defense.","flavorText":"The 23rd Division, aka Sunrise Division, of the Imperial Japanese Army was formed in 1938 during the outbreak of the Second Sino-Japanese War (1937-1945). The division participated in the Battle of Khalkhin Gol against the Red Army in 1939, where it suffered a staggering loss of 12,000 men, which was about 80% of their combat strength. Following the devastating defeat the remnants of the division returned to Japan to assist with the border defense force, but was later reformed as a mechanized infantry division and sent to Taiwan for garrison duties in 1944. That same year the Sunrise Division was sent to the Philippines where it participated in the Battle of Luzon, against the US and Philippine Commonwealth forces, where it lost 24,508 men out of a total strength of 29,636 men. After the Battle of Luzon the Sunrise Division ceased to exist.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_sunrise_division","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_sunrise_division_title","SourceString":"SUNRISE DIVISION","LocalizedString":"SUNRISE DIVISION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_sunrise_division_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Gets +6+6 if your HQ has 10 or less defense.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Gets +6+6 if your HQ has 10 or less defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_sunrise_division_history","SourceString":"The 23rd Division, aka Sunrise Division, of the Imperial Japanese Army was formed in 1938 during the outbreak of the Second Sino-Japanese War (1937-1945). The division participated in the Battle of Khalkhin Gol against the Red Army in 1939, where it suffered a staggering loss of 12,000 men, which was about 80% of their combat strength. Following the devastating defeat the remnants of the division returned to Japan to assist with the border defense force, but was later reformed as a mechanized infantry division and sent to Taiwan for garrison duties in 1944. That same year the Sunrise Division was sent to the Philippines where it participated in the Battle of Luzon, against the US and Philippine Commonwealth forces, where it lost 24,508 men out of a total strength of 29,636 men. After the Battle of Luzon the Sunrise Division ceased to exist.","LocalizedString":"The 23rd Division, aka Sunrise Division, of the Imperial Japanese Army was formed in 1938 during the outbreak of the Second Sino-Japanese War (1937-1945). The division participated in the Battle of Khalkhin Gol against the Red Army in 1939, where it suffered a staggering loss of 12,000 men, which was about 80% of their combat strength. Following the devastating defeat the remnants of the division returned to Japan to assist with the border defense force, but was later reformed as a mechanized infantry division and sent to Taiwan for garrison duties in 1944. That same year the Sunrise Division was sent to the Philippines where it participated in the Battle of Luzon, against the US and Philippine Commonwealth forces, where it lost 24,508 men out of a total strength of 29,636 men. After the Battle of Luzon the Sunrise Division ceased to exist."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Infantry_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Infantry_Move_FX.0"},"soundMo